From e4ae4187a22429e47cc2286f487869f1e01d1349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "opus-pr2-patch (Claude)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:03:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] history: a listed shard missing on disk becomes unknown,
 not zero (D-1)

archive_observations visited only days present on disk or in the incoming
run record (history.py:382), so a day whose indexed shard had vanished was
never checked and the row builder (history.py:470-476) wrote count 0 with
coverage full for a day that had archived flashes. A missing hourly part
produced a silent undercount (count 4 of 8, coverage full).

Days listed in the previous index are now visited too. If any listed file
is missing, the day is marked shard_lost: coverage none, scanned_seconds 0,
count null. The flag is sticky, so flashes for that day arriving later are
dropped (counted in dropped_lost_day) rather than rebuilding a partial
count. Remaining files are left untouched and unlisted for manual recovery.

Tests: test_listed_shard_missing_on_disk_becomes_unknown_not_zero,
test_missing_hourly_part_marks_the_whole_day_unknown (both fail at f7db76c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
